# Repository-wide ignores. backend/ and mobile/ keep their own for tool-specific
# artefacts; this covers everything shared and everything dangerous.

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the database password, the JWT secret and the Razorpay key secret.
# The .example files are committed; the real ones never are.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
# EAS credentials, if ever downloaded locally
credentials.json

# --- dependencies and build output -------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Expo --------------------------------------------------------------------
.expo/
.expo-shared/
expo-env.d.ts.bak
# Continuous Native Generation rebuilds these; committing them defeats the point
# and guarantees merge conflicts.
/mobile/android/
/mobile/ios/

# --- editors and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
# .vscode is kept: the Expo template ships shared editor settings worth sharing

# --- logs and local scratch --------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.local


app-reference-images
# --- local reference material ------------------------------------------------
# Large, local, and not part of the build. 60MB between them, and git keeps
# every byte forever once committed.
#
#   assets/                 source images, before optimising. docs/asset-contract.md
#                           §1 is explicit that source files live OUTSIDE this
#                           repo — the optimised output is what ships, and for
#                           room backdrops that is backend/public/ (220KB).
#   app-reference-images/   competitor screenshots the room UI was built from.
#                           Keep them; they are referenced by
#                           docs/room-ui-reference-report.md and are the thing
#                           to re-read before changing room layout. They are also
#                           somebody else's app, which is its own reason not to
#                           redistribute them in a repo.
#   reference-assets/       the same, for art.
#
# None of these are deleted — they stay on disk. If you would rather version
# them, use a bucket or git-lfs rather than the repo.
assets/
app-reference-images/
reference-assets/
